= Authorization =

== Overview ==
'''Authorization''' is the process or policy decision that determines whether a subject is permitted to perform an action on a resource under defined rules.

Authorization is commonly evaluated after authentication, but systems can also authorize anonymous or capability-bearing requests without conventional user authentication. Decisions can depend on roles, attributes, relationships, ownership, context, or explicit capabilities.

Authentication establishes who or what a claimant is within a system; authorization determines permitted actions.

== Boundaries ==
* authorization ≠ authentication
* authorization ≠ identity
* access decision ≠ proof of legitimacy outside the policy

